  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "If each number in a set of ten numbers is increased by \\(20,\\) the arithmetic mean (average) of the original ten numbers:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "remains the same",
    "B": "is increased by \\(20\\)",
    "C": "is increased by \\(200\\)",
    "D": "is increased by \\(10\\)",
    "E": "is increased by \\(2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The mean is the total divided by the number of entries. Adding 20 to each of 10 numbers increases their total by \\(10\\cdot20=200\\). Since there are still 10 numbers, the mean increases by\n\\[\n\\frac{200}{10}=\\boxed{20}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\text{B}\\).",
